The per-frame PRESENT gate DGROUP:0x738 (c738) is a BYTE, not undefined2 -- Ghidra's word typing
disables the whole present body during the menu idle loop.

FUN_1000_31c3 (the present) gates its body -- the async retrace/palette upload (pcRam0001c5e4 = MGAVIDEO
0b1f), the mouse-cursor position copy (FUN_1000_3a00: dd9e/dda0 -> d5ca/d5cc), the cursor DRAW (d5b0) and
the frame blit (c2b0) -- on `c738++; if (c738 == 0)`.  The asm is `inc BYTE ds:0x738; jne <skip>` (verified
at 0x131cc) and the normal resting value is 0xff (-1), so the byte inc 0xff->0x00 sets ZF and the body
RUNS.  Ghidra typed DAT_1000_c738 as undefined2 (WORD); the live word is 0x00ff (high byte c739 = 0), so
the C computes 0x00ff + 1 = 0x0100 != 0 and the body is ALWAYS SKIPPED.  That is why, during the menu
idle, the cursor never redraws from the mouse position and the palette needed the shim retrace workaround
(patch 117): the entire present body was dead.  Retype c738 to its true byte width so the inc/compare
matches the asm (0xff -> 0 -> body runs).  The 30f8 `if (c738 == -1)` folded from `inc BYTE; jne` reads the
resting 0xff; undefined1 is unsigned (uint8_t) so `== -1` (int -1) never matches -> compare against 0xff.
Same store/load-width Ghidra class as patches 104/105/106.  Asm-verified against FUN_1000_31c3 (0x131c3),
FUN_1000_30f8 (0x130f8) and FUN_1000_3218.  c739 (0x739) is not a separate symbol -> byte-typing is safe.
